  "articlePanels": [{"kind":"lede","html":"<p>Joblogic is a full field-service management platform. So the honest reason to look for a <strong>joblogic alternative uk</strong> teams will use is usually not that Joblogic is weak. It is that Joblogic is a large, complete platform, and some teams do not need the whole thing. They just need inspections and compliance captured on site.</p><p>Here is a fair comparison, where Joblogic is the right choice, and where a no-app capture layer wins.</p>"},{"kind":"takeaways","heading":"The short version","html":"<ul><li>Joblogic is a mature, full-featured field-service management platform: planned maintenance, scheduling, dispatch, asset management, quotes and invoicing. Pricing is per-user and quote-based, at the platform end of the market.</li><li>If you need to run a whole maintenance or service operation end to end, Joblogic is the right category and does it well. We say that plainly.</li><li>Quickler is not a smaller, cheaper Joblogic. It is a different category: the no-app layer that captures inspections and compliance records on site.</li><li>Quickler runs in the worker's existing WhatsApp chat. No app, no login.</li><li>Quickler is £20 per active user a month, dormant users free, only pay for who works, everything unlimited on a paid account.</li><li>Pricing figures for Joblogic are approximate and quote-based. Check their current pricing before deciding.</li></ul>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"Credit where due","heading":"What Joblogic does well","html":"<p>An honest comparison starts where the product is strong, and Joblogic is strong across a lot of ground.</p><p>It is a genuine end-to-end platform. Planned and reactive maintenance, scheduling and dispatch, asset and contract management, mobile job sheets, quoting and invoicing all live in one system. For a service or maintenance business that wants a single source of truth for the whole operation, that breadth is the point, and few lightweight tools come close.</p><p>It is UK-built, with support and onboarding geared to larger, more complex rollouts, which is appropriate for a platform of this scope. If you run a maintenance contractor, an FM operation or a wider field-service business and need to manage the whole job lifecycle, Joblogic is a serious, capable choice. None of that is in doubt.</p>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"The real difference","heading":"It is a platform, not a capture layer","html":"<p>The difference between Joblogic and Quickler is not that one is better. It is that they are different categories. Joblogic manages the whole operation. Quickler captures one thing well: inspections and compliance records, on site, without an app.</p><p>Joblogic has a mobile app for field staff, like any full FSM platform. That app carries the whole job context, which is powerful, but it is still an app to open and a login to keep alive. For inspection and compliance capture specifically, that is the same on-site friction any app has. The check gets done, the app gets filled in later from memory, and the record reflects what someone remembered.</p><p>Quickler does not try to replace field-service management. If that is what you need, Joblogic is the right answer and a capture layer will not stand in for it. Quickler solves the narrower problem of getting the on-site record captured reliably in the first place.</p>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"The alternatives","heading":"Platforms, paper, and WhatsApp","html":"<p><strong>Joblogic</strong> is the full field-service platform: plan, schedule, dispatch, invoice, all in one. Pick it when you need to run the whole operation, not just inspections. It is the right category for that job.</p><p><strong>Paper and spreadsheets</strong> stay common in UK teams. Free, familiar, no training. The records are illegible, unsearchable, and impossible to produce when a client or regulator asks. The cost is not the subscription. It is the liability when the folder cannot be found.</p><p><strong>Quickler</strong> removes the app for the capture step. The inspection workflow arrives in the worker's existing WhatsApp chat and they reply to each question as a message. Same behaviour they already do all day, no install, no login. The tradeoff is that quickler is not a field-service platform and does not try to be.</p>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"The no-app option","heading":"Quickler, and where it stops","html":"<p>Quickler runs in WhatsApp. Nothing to install, no login. The inspection or compliance workflow arrives in the worker's existing WhatsApp chat, and they reply to each question as a message. Voice notes are transcribed automatically. The core output is a shareable web report and a permanent record, with optional PDF and CSV export. Pricing is only for active users: [[price:bundles]]. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, so you add your whole team and only pay for who actually works. Everything is unlimited on a paid account, so anyone who reads but never files adds nothing to the cost.</p><p>The honest limit: quickler is not field-service management software. It does not plan maintenance, schedule engineers, manage assets or invoice jobs. If you need any of that, Joblogic is the more complete product and there is no contest. Quickler is built for teams of roughly 1 to 30 doing structured compliance and inspection capture. It serves care homes, nurseries, schools, estates, cleaning firms and trades, anyone who inspects or keeps records. Rooted in UK compliance, it works anywhere WhatsApp does. If you need to run the whole operation in one system, Joblogic is the right tool. If you just need the on-site record captured, that is what quickler does.</p>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"Scope, install, price","heading":"Direct comparison","html":"<table><thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Scope</th><th>App install?</th><th>Pricing model</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Joblogic</td><td>Full field-service management</td><td>Yes, login required</td><td>Per user, quote-based</td></tr><tr><td>SimPro</td><td>Full job management and FSM</td><td>Yes, login required</td><td>Quote-based, platform tier</td></tr><tr><td>Fergus</td><td>Job, quote and invoice management</td><td>Yes, login required</td><td>Per user subscription</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Quickler</strong></td><td><strong>Inspection and compliance capture</strong></td><td><strong>No, WhatsApp only</strong></td><td><strong>£20 per active user/mo, dormant users free</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Pricing is approximate and, for the platforms, quote-based. Check each vendor's current pricing before deciding. The deciding test is simple: do you need to run the whole service operation, or just capture inspections reliably on site? If the former, Joblogic is the right category. If the latter, a WhatsApp-native workflow removes the app barrier because your team already uses WhatsApp. See <a href=\"/pages/simpro-alternative-uk.html\">SimPro alternative UK</a> and <a href=\"/pages/fergus-alternative-uk.html\">Fergus alternative UK</a>.</p>"},{"kind":"faq","heading":"Questions, answered","html":"<h3>Is Joblogic any good?</h3><p>Yes. Joblogic is a mature, UK-built field-service management platform covering planned maintenance, scheduling, dispatch, asset management, quotes and invoicing. If you need to run a whole service operation in one system, it is a serious, capable choice. We would not tell you otherwise.</p><h3>What is the difference between Joblogic and Quickler?</h3><p>They are different categories. Joblogic is a full field-service platform that runs the whole operation. Quickler is a lightweight capture layer that gets inspections and compliance records captured on site, in WhatsApp, with no app and no login. Quickler does not do scheduling or invoicing and is not trying to replace Joblogic.</p><h3>Is Quickler cheaper than Joblogic?</h3><p>They are not really comparable on price because they do different jobs. Joblogic is a platform priced per user by quote. Quickler charges £20 per active user a month, where an active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, and dormant users are free. If all you need is inspection capture, quickler is far lighter and cheaper. If you need full field-service management, Joblogic is doing much more for the money.</p><h3>Should I switch from Joblogic to Quickler?</h3><p>Usually not as a straight swap, because they do different things. If you rely on Joblogic for scheduling, assets and invoicing, keep it. Many teams add quickler alongside it purely for on-site inspection and compliance capture, so the record gets caught reliably without another app. Quickler has a free tier of 20 reports a month, up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock. Related: <a href=\"/pages/simpro-alternative-uk.html\">SimPro alternative UK</a> and <a href=\"/pages/alternatives.html\">all comparisons</a>.</p>"}],
