  "seoBody": "<h2>Is Joblogic a good product?</h2><p>Yes. We will say that plainly. Joblogic is a mature, UK-built field-service management platform. Planned maintenance, scheduling, dispatch, asset management, quoting and invoicing all live in one system, and for a service business that wants a single source of truth across the whole operation, that breadth is the point.</p><p>So the honest reason firms go looking for a Joblogic alternative is rarely that Joblogic is weak. It is that Joblogic is a large, complete platform, and some teams do not need the whole thing. They just need inspections and compliance captured reliably on site.</p><h2>The real difference</h2><p>Joblogic and Quickler are different categories. Joblogic manages the whole operation. Quickler captures one thing well: inspections and compliance records, on site, without an app.</p><p>Joblogic has a mobile app for field staff, as any full FSM platform does, and it carries the whole job context. For inspection capture specifically, that is still an app to open and a login to keep alive. The check gets done, the app gets filled in later from memory, and the record reflects what someone remembered rather than what they observed.</p><p>Quickler does not try to replace field-service management. If that is what you need, Joblogic is the right answer and a capture layer will not stand in for it.</p><h2>The alternatives</h2><h3>Joblogic</h3><p>The full field-service platform: plan, schedule, dispatch, invoice, all in one. Pick it when you need to run the whole operation, not just inspections. It is the right category for that job and few lightweight tools come close.</p><h3>Paper and spreadsheets</h3><p>Still common in UK teams. Free, familiar, no training. The records are illegible, unsearchable, and impossible to produce when a client or regulator asks. The cost is not the subscription. It is the liability when the folder cannot be found.</p><h3>Quickler</h3><p>Quickler runs in WhatsApp. There is nothing to install and no login. The inspection or compliance workflow arrives in the worker's existing WhatsApp chat, and they reply to each question as a message, the same way they reply to anything else. Voice notes are transcribed automatically. The core output is a shareable web report and a permanent record, with optional PDF and CSV export.</p><p>Pricing is only for active users: [[price:bundles]]. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, so you add your whole team and only pay for who actually works. Everything is unlimited on a paid account.</p><p>The honest limitation: quickler is not field-service management software. It does not plan maintenance, schedule engineers, manage assets or invoice jobs. For any of that, Joblogic is the more complete product. Quickler is built for teams of roughly 1 to 30 doing structured compliance and inspection capture, and it serves care homes, nurseries, schools, estates, cleaning firms and trades, anyone who inspects or keeps records. Rooted in UK compliance, it works anywhere WhatsApp does.</p><h2>Direct comparison</h2><p><strong>Joblogic:</strong> full field-service management; app install and login required; per-user, quote-based.</p><p><strong>SimPro:</strong> full job management and FSM; app install and login required; quote-based pricing at the platform tier.</p><p><strong>Fergus:</strong> job, quote and invoice management; app install and login required; per-user subscription.</p><p><strong>Quickler:</strong> inspection and compliance capture; £20 per active user/mo, dormant users free, only pay for who works; WhatsApp only, no install; UK-based, direct founder contact.</p><p>Pricing is approximate and, for the platforms, quote-based. Check each vendor's current pricing before deciding.</p><h2>How to choose</h2><p>The deciding test is simple: do you need to run the whole service operation, or just capture inspections reliably on site?</p><p>If you need to plan maintenance, schedule engineers, manage assets and invoice jobs, Joblogic is the right category and a capture layer will not replace it.</p><p>If your problem is narrower, that inspections and compliance checks are not being captured reliably because opening an app on site is one step too many, a WhatsApp-native workflow removes the barrier because your team already uses WhatsApp for everything else.</p><p><strong>One thing to check before deciding:</strong> many teams run both, an FSM platform for the operation and quickler for the on-site record. They are not mutually exclusive.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is Joblogic any good?</h3><p>Yes. Joblogic is a mature, UK-built field-service management platform covering planned maintenance, scheduling, dispatch, asset management, quotes and invoicing. If you need to run a whole service operation in one system, it is a serious, capable choice.</p><h3>What is the difference between Joblogic and Quickler?</h3><p>They are different categories. Joblogic is a full field-service platform that runs the whole operation. Quickler is a lightweight capture layer that gets inspections and compliance records captured on site, in WhatsApp, with no app and no login. Quickler does not do scheduling or invoicing.</p><h3>Is Quickler cheaper than Joblogic?</h3><p>They are not really comparable on price because they do different jobs. Joblogic is a platform priced per user by quote. Quickler charges £20 per active user a month, where an active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, and dormant users are free. If all you need is inspection capture, quickler is far lighter and cheaper. If you need full field-service management, Joblogic is doing much more.</p><h3>Should I switch from Joblogic to Quickler?</h3><p>Usually not as a straight swap, because they do different things. If you rely on Joblogic for scheduling, assets and invoicing, keep it. Many teams add quickler alongside it purely for on-site inspection and compliance capture. Quickler has a free tier of 20 reports a month, up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock.</p><h2>Try this in Quickler</h2><p>Start free, no card, no trial clock. Copy and paste this into the workflow description when you sign up at <a href=\"https://app.quickler.co/signup\">app.quickler.co/signup</a>:</p><p><code>Joblogic alternative for inspection capture. Workflow name: [Your inspection or compliance check name]. Description: Describe the on-site check you need captured. Include: what is being inspected, number of questions, whether photos are required, and what the output looks like. Quickler builds it as a WhatsApp workflow. £20 per active user a month, dormant users free, only pay for who works.</code></p><p>Quickler reads your description and builds the WhatsApp question sequence. Your team answers on site. Report produced automatically.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/simpro-alternative-uk.html\">SimPro alternative UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/fergus-alternative-uk.html\">Fergus alternative UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/fieldwire-alternative-uk.html\">Fieldwire alternative UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/alternatives.html\">All comparisons</a></li></ul>",
